		"title": "Which maps preserve the Gram matrix",
		"html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Which maps preserve the Gram matrix?</title>\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --blue:#2563eb; --blue-d:#1d4ed8;\n    --orange:#ea7317; --orange-d:#c2410c;\n    --ink:#111827; --muted:#6b7280; --line:#e5e7eb;\n    --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  }\n  *{box-sizing:border-box;}\n  html,body{margin:0;background:#ffffff;}\n  body{\n    color:var(--ink);\n    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;\n  }\n  .wrap{max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:18px 22px 28px;}\n  h1{font-size:19px;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 3px;letter-spacing:-.01em;}\n  .sub{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 14px;}\n\n  .panels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;}\n  .card{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:10px 12px 12px;}\n  .ptitle{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 6px;}\n  .ptitle.blue{color:var(--blue);}\n  .ptitle.orange{color:var(--orange);}\n  canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:300px;}\n\n  .controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:14px;}\n  .label{\n    font-size:11.5px;font-weight:650;color:#374151;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;\n    display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;margin-bottom:8px;\n  }\n  .val{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink);text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-weight:700;}\n  .modes{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;}\n  .mode{\n    font:inherit;font-size:12px;padding:5px 10px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--line);\n    background:#fff;color:#374151;cursor:pointer;\n  }\n  .mode:hover{border-color:#cbd5e1;background:#f8fafc;}\n  .mode.active{background:var(--blue);border-color:var(--blue);color:#fff;font-weight:650;}\n  input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--blue);margin:3px 0 0;display:block;}\n  .card.disabled{opacity:.4;}\n  .card.disabled input[type=range]{pointer-events:none;}\n  .det{\n    display:inline-block;margin-top:10px;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:7px;\n    background:#eff6ff;border:1px solid #dbeafe;font-size:12px;color:#1e3a8a;\n  }\n  .det b{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;color:var(--blue-d);}\n\n  .row2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:250px 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:12px;}\n  .qmat{\n    display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2px 12px;width:max-content;\n    border-left:2px solid #9ca3af;border-right:2px solid #9ca3af;padding:4px 10px;\n    font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13.5px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n  }\n  .qmat span{text-align:right;}\n  .qdet{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px;}\n\n  .btnrow{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;}\n  .btn{\n    font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;padding:6px 11px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\n    background:#fff;cursor:pointer;color:#111827;\n  }\n  .btn:hover{background:#f3f4f6;}\n  .btn.alt{border-style:dashed;color:#4b5563;}\n\n  .readouts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:12px;}\n  .blabel{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:650;color:#374151;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-bottom:2px;}\n  .bnum{font-size:34px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;line-height:1.1;}\n  .bnum.zero{color:var(--blue);}\n  .bnum.nonzero{color:var(--orange);}\n  .bsub{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:4px;}\n\n  .grams{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto auto 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:12px;align-items:start;}\n  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6, 30px);gap:2px;}\n  .cell{\n    width:30px;height:26px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;\n    font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;border-radius:3px;cursor:crosshair;user-select:none;\n  }\n  .cell.hl{outline:2px solid #111827;outline-offset:-2px;}\n  .hint{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:8px;}\n\n  .verdict{font-size:16px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;margin:0;}\n  .verdict.ok{color:var(--blue-d);}\n  .verdict.bad{color:var(--orange-d);}\n  .vsub{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;color:#374151;margin-top:8px;}\n  .vsub b{color:var(--ink);}\n  .caption{\n    margin-top:14px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid var(--line);\n    font-size:12.5px;color:#374151;line-height:1.5;\n  }\n  .tip{\n    position:fixed;z-index:99;pointer-events:none;display:none;\n    background:#111827;color:#fff;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;\n    padding:6px 9px;border-radius:7px;line-height:1.5;white-space:nowrap;\n    box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.22);\n  }\n  .tip b{color:#fff;}\n  @media (max-width:900px){\n    .panels{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n    .controls{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}\n    .row2{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n    .readouts{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n    .grams{grid-template-columns:auto auto;}\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <h1>Which maps preserve the Gram matrix?</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">A configuration is only its Gram matrix K = X Xᵀ. Both panels share the same scale.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"panels\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"ptitle blue\">Original points</div>\n      <canvas id=\"cvA\"></canvas>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"ptitle orange\">After Q</div>\n      <canvas id=\"cvB\"></canvas>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Mode</div>\n      <div class=\"modes\">\n        <button class=\"mode active\" data-mode=\"rotation\">rotation</button>\n        <button class=\"mode\" data-mode=\"shear\">shear</button>\n        <button class=\"mode\" data-mode=\"scaling\">scaling</button>\n        <button class=\"mode\" data-mode=\"rotshear\">rotation × shear</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\" id=\"ctlTheta\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Rotation angle θ <span class=\"val\" id=\"thetaVal\">30°</span></div>\n      <input type=\"range\" id=\"theta\" min=\"0\" max=\"360\" step=\"1\" value=\"30\">\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\" id=\"ctlShear\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Shear s <span class=\"val\" id=\"shearVal\">0.80</span></div>\n      <input type=\"range\" id=\"shear\" min=\"-1.5\" max=\"1.5\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.8\">\n      <div class=\"det\">det S = <b id=\"detS\">1.00</b> &nbsp;always</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"card\" id=\"ctlScale\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Scale k <span class=\"val\" id=\"scaleVal\">1.00</span></div>\n      <input type=\"range\" id=\"scale\" min=\"0.5\" max=\"2\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"1\">\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"row2\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Applied matrix Q</div>\n      <div class=\"qmat\">\n        <span id=\"q00\">1.000</span><span id=\"q01\">0.000</span>\n        <span id=\"q10\">0.000</span><span id=\"q11\">1.000</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"qdet\" id=\"qdet\">det Q = 1.000</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"label\">Presets &amp; points</div>\n      <div class=\"btnrow\">\n        <button class=\"btn\" data-preset=\"rot37\">rotation 37°</button>\n        <button class=\"btn\" data-preset=\"shear08\">shear 0.8 (det = 1)</button>\n        <button class=\"btn\" data-preset=\"rotshear\">det = 1 rotation-then-shear</button>\n        <button class=\"btn alt\" id=\"randomBtn\">randomize points</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"hint\">The shear matrix is S = [[1, s], [0, 1]]; its determinant is 1 for every s.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"readouts\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"blabel\">Max relative change in the Gram matrix</div>\n      <div class=\"bnum zero\" id=\"gramChange\">0.00%</div>\n      <div class=\"bsub\">max<sub>ij</sub> |K′<sub>ij</sub> − K<sub>ij</sub>| / max<sub>ij</sub> |K<sub>ij</sub>|</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"blabel\">Max relative change in pairwise distances</div>\n      <div class=\"bnum zero\" id=\"distChange\">0.00%</div>\n      <div class=\"bsub\">max<sub>ij</sub> |d′<sub>ij</sub> − d<sub>ij</sub>| / max<sub>ij</sub> d<sub>ij</sub></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"grams\">\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"label\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">K = X Xᵀ <span style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;color:#6b7280;font-weight:500\">original</span></div>\n      <div class=\"grid\" id=\"gridK\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\">\n      <div class=\"label\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">K′ = X′ X′ᵀ <span style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;color:#6b7280;font-weight:500\">after Q</span></div>\n      <div class=\"grid\" id=\"gridK2\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"card\" style=\"align-self:stretch\">\n      <p class=\"verdict ok\" id=\"verdict\">This map is orthogonal: it preserves every distance and the whole Gram matrix</p>\n      <div class=\"vsub\" id=\"vsub\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n      <div class=\"hint\">Hover any cell of either heatmap to compare K<sub>ij</sub> with K′<sub>ij</sub>. Rows and columns are the points A–F in order.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"caption\">\n    <b>det(Q) = 1 does not imply that distances are preserved.</b>\n    The shear S = [[1, s], [0, 1]] has det S = 1 for every value of s, yet it changes pairwise distances and the Gram matrix\n    — use the preset “shear 0.8 (det = 1)” to see the counterexample. What actually preserves all pairwise geometry is\n    orthogonality: QᵀQ = I.\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"tip\" id=\"tip\"></div>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n  'use strict';\n\n  var $ = function(id){ return document.getElementById(id); };\n  var LABELS = ['A','B','C','D','E','F'];\n  var N = 6;\n  var DEFAULT_POINTS = [[1,0.5],[2,1.8],[1.6,2.4],[0.6,1.2],[2.4,0.9],[1.1,2.0]];\n\n  var points = DEFAULT_POINTS.map(function(p){ return p.slice(); });\n  var state = { mode:'rotation', theta:30, shear:0.8, scale:1 };\n  var current = { Q:[[1,0],[0,1]], P2:points.map(function(p){return p.slice();}), K:null, K2:null };\n  var view = { cx:1.5, cy:1.5, half:3, init:false };\n\n  /* ---------------- linear algebra helpers ---------------- */\n  function mul(A,B){\n    var C = [[0,0],[0,0]];\n    for(var i=0;i<2;i++) for(var j=0;j<2;j++){\n      var s=0; for(var k=0;k<2;k++) s += A[i][k]*B[k][j];\n      C[i][j]=s;\n    }\n    return C;\n  }\n  function applyQ(Q,p){\n    return [ Q[0][0]*p[0] + Q[0][1]*p[1], Q[1][0]*p[0] + Q[1][1]*p[1] ];\n  }\n  function getQ(){\n    var t = state.theta*Math.PI/180;\n    var c = Math.cos(t), s = Math.sin(t);\n    var R  = [[c,-s],[s,c]];\n    var S  = [[1,state.shear],[0,1]];\n    var Sc = [[state.scale,0],[0,state.scale]];\n    if(state.mode === 'rotation') return R;\n    if(state.mode === 'shear')    return S;\n    if(state.mode === 'scaling')  return Sc;\n    return mul(S,R);            /* rotate first, then shear */\n  }\n  function gram(P){\n    var K=[];\n    for(var i=0;i<N;i++){\n      var row=[];\n      for(var j=0;j<N;j++) row.push(P[i][0]*P[j][0] + P[i][1]*P[j][1]);\n      K.push(row);\n    }\n    return K;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- DOM refs ---------------- */\n  var cvA=$('cvA'), cvB=$('cvB');\n  var thetaEl=$('theta'), shearEl=$('shear'), scaleEl=$('scale');\n  var thetaVal=$('thetaVal'), shearVal=$('shearVal'), scaleVal=$('scaleVal'), detSEl=$('detS');\n  var ctlTheta=$('ctlTheta'), ctlShear=$('ctlShear'), ctlScale=$('ctlScale');\n  var gridK=$('gridK'), gridK2=$('gridK2');\n  var tip=$('tip');\n  var cellsK=[], cellsK2=[];\n\n  var modeBtns = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.mode'));\n  var presetBtns = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-preset]'));\n\n  /* ---------------- heatmap cells (built once) ---------------- */\n  function initHeatmap(el, store){\n    el.innerHTML='';\n    for(var i=0;i<N;i++) for(var j=0;j<N;j++){\n      var d=document.createElement('div');\n      d.className='cell';\n      d.dataset.i=String(i);\n      d.dataset.j=String(j);\n      el.appendChild(d);\n      store.push(d);\n    }\n  }\n  initHeatmap(gridK, cellsK);\n  initHeatmap(gridK2, cellsK2);\n\n  function fmtCell(v){\n    if(Math.abs(v) >= 100) return v.toFixed(0);\n    return v.toFixed(1);\n  }\n  function paint(store, M, maxAbs, hue, sat){\n    for(var i=0;i<N;i++) for(var j=0;j<N;j++){\n      var v = M[i][j];\n      var t = maxAbs>0 ? Math.min(1, Math.abs(v)/maxAbs) : 0;\n      var c = store[i*N+j];\n      c.style.background = 'hsl(' + hue + ', ' + sat + '%, ' + (94 - 52*t).toFixed(1) + '%)';\n      c.style.color = (t>0.55) ? '#ffffff' : '#1f2430';\n      c.textContent = fmtCell(v);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- tooltip on hover ---------------- */\n  var hlIdx = -1;\n  function clearHl(){\n    if(hlIdx>=0){\n      cellsK[hlIdx].classList.remove('hl');\n      cellsK2[hlIdx].classList.remove('hl');\n      hlIdx = -1;\n    }\n  }\n  function onMove(e){\n    var c = e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.cell') : null;\n    if(!c){ tip.style.display='none'; clearHl(); return; }\n    var i = +c.dataset.i, j = +c.dataset.j, idx = i*N+j;\n    if(idx !== hlIdx){\n      clearHl();\n      cellsK[idx].classList.add('hl');\n      cellsK2[idx].classList.add('hl');\n      hlIdx = idx;\n    }\n    var k = current.K[i][j], k2 = current.K2[i][j];\n    tip.innerHTML = '<div>K<sub>'+LABELS[i]+LABELS[j]+'</sub> = '+k.toFixed(3)+'</div>' +\n                    '<div>K′<sub>'+LABELS[i]+LABELS[j]+'</sub> = '+k2.toFixed(3)+'</div>' +\n                    '<div style=\"opacity:.7\">Δ = '+(k2-k).toFixed(3)+'</div>';\n    tip.style.display='block';\n    var x = e.clientX + 14, y = e.clientY + 14;\n    var w = tip.offsetWidth, h = tip.offsetHeight;\n    if(x + w > window.innerWidth - 8) x = e.clientX - w - 14;\n    if(y + h > window.innerHeight - 8) y = e.clientY - h - 14;\n    tip.style.left = Math.max(6,x) + 'px';\n    tip.style.top  = Math.max(6,y) + 'px';\n  }\n  gridK.addEventListener('mousemove', onMove);\n  gridK2.addEventListener('mousemove', onMove);\n  gridK.addEventListener('mouseleave', function(){ tip.style.display='none'; clearHl(); });\n  gridK2.addEventListener('mouseleave', function(){ tip.style.display='none'; clearHl(); });\n\n  /* ---------------- main update ---------------- */\n  var ACTIVE = {\n    rotation: { theta:true,  shear:false, scale:false },\n    shear:    { theta:false, shear:true,  scale:false },\n    scaling:  { theta:false, shear:false, scale:true  },\n    rotshear: { theta:true,  shear:true,  scale:false }\n  };\n\n  function syncUI(){\n    thetaEl.value = state.theta;\n    shearEl.value = state.shear;\n    scaleEl.value = state.scale;\n    thetaVal.textContent = state.theta.toFixed(0) + '°';\n    shearVal.textContent = state.shear.toFixed(2);\n    scaleVal.textContent = state.scale.toFixed(2);\n    detSEl.textContent = (1*1 - state.shear*0).toFixed(2);\n\n    modeBtns.forEach(function(b){ b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.mode === state.mode); });\n\n    var a = ACTIVE[state.mode];\n    ctlTheta.classList.toggle('disabled', !a.theta);\n    ctlShear.classList.toggle('disabled', !a.shear);\n    ctlScale.classList.toggle('disabled', !a.scale);\n    thetaEl.disabled = !a.theta;\n    shearEl.disabled = !a.shear;\n    scaleEl.disabled = !a.scale;\n  }\n\n  function num(v){\n    var r = (Math.abs(v) < 5e-4) ? 0 : v;\n    return r.toFixed(3);\n  }\n\n  function update(){\n    var Q = getQ();\n    var P2 = points.map(function(p){ return applyQ(Q,p); });\n    var K = gram(points), K2 = gram(P2);\n    current = { Q:Q, P2:P2, K:K, K2:K2 };\n\n    /* --- Gram change --- */\n    var maxK = 0, maxGdiff = 0, i, j;\n    for(i=0;i<N;i++) for(j=0;j<N;j++){\n      if(Math.abs(K[i][j]) > maxK) maxK = Math.abs(K[i][j]);\n      var dg = Math.abs(K2[i][j]-K[i][j]);\n      if(dg > maxGdiff) maxGdiff = dg;\n    }\n    var gramRel = maxK > 0 ? maxGdiff/maxK : 0;\n\n    /* --- distance change --- */\n    var maxD = 0, maxDdiff = 0;\n    for(i=0;i<N;i++) for(j=i+1;j<N;j++){\n      var d0 = Math.hypot(points[i][0]-points[j][0], points[i][1]-points[j][1]);\n      var d1 = Math.hypot(P2[i][0]-P2[j][0], P2[i][1]-P2[j][1]);\n      if(d0 > maxD) maxD = d0;\n      var dd = Math.abs(d1-d0);\n      if(dd > maxDdiff) maxDdiff = dd;\n    }\n    var distRel = maxD > 0 ? maxDdiff/maxD : 0;\n\n    /* --- orthogonality --- */\n    var QtQ = mul([[Q[0][0],Q[1][0]],[Q[0][1],Q[1][1]]], Q);\n    var frob2 = 0;\n    for(i=0;i<2;i++) for(j=0;j<2;j++){\n      var t = QtQ[i][j] - (i===j?1:0);\n      frob2 += t*t;\n    }\n    var frob = Math.sqrt(frob2);\n    var orth = frob <= 1e-9;\n    var detQ = Q[0][0]*Q[1][1] - Q[0][1]*Q[1][0];\n    var QtIsc = Math.abs(QtQ[0][0]-1)+Math.abs(QtQ[1][1]-1)+Math.abs(QtQ[0][1])+Math.abs(QtQ[1][0]);\n\n    /* --- DOM: matrix --- */\n    $('q00').textContent = num(Q[0][0]);\n    $('q01').textContent = num(Q[0][1]);\n    $('q10').textContent = num(Q[1][0]);\n    $('q11').textContent = num(Q[1][1]);\n    $('qdet').textContent = 'det Q = ' + detQ.toFixed(3);\n\n    /* --- DOM: big readouts --- */\n    var gEl = $('gramChange'), dEl = $('distChange');\n    gEl.textContent = (100*gramRel).toFixed(2) + '%';\n    dEl.textContent = (100*distRel).toFixed(2) + '%';\n    gEl.className = 'bnum ' + (gramRel <= 1e-9 ? 'zero' : 'nonzero');\n    dEl.className = 'bnum ' + (distRel <= 1e-9 ? 'zero' : 'nonzero');\n\n    /* --- DOM: verdict --- */\n    var v = $('verdict'), sub = $('vsub');\n    if(orth){\n      v.textContent = 'This map is orthogonal: it preserves every distance and the whole Gram matrix';\n      v.className = 'verdict ok';\n      sub.style.display = 'none';\n    } else {\n      v.textContent = 'This map is NOT orthogonal: distances change';\n      v.className = 'verdict bad';\n      sub.style.display = 'block';\n      sub.innerHTML = '‖QᵀQ − I‖<sub>F</sub> = <b>' + frob.toFixed(4) + '</b>' +\n                      ' &nbsp;·&nbsp; det(Q) = <b>' + detQ.toFixed(4) + '</b>' +\n                      ' &nbsp;·&nbsp; ‖QᵀQ − I‖<sub>max</sub> = <b>' + QtIsc.toFixed(4) + '</b>';\n    }\n\n    /* --- DOM: heatmaps --- */\n    var maxAbs = 0;\n    for(i=0;i<N;i++) for(j=0;j<N;j++) maxAbs = Math.max(maxAbs, Math.abs(K[i][j]), Math.abs(K2[i][j]));\n    paint(cellsK,  K,  maxAbs, 220, 76);\n    paint(cellsK2, K2, maxAbs, 28,  84);\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- drawing ---------------- */\n  function computeTargetView(){\n    var all = points.concat(current.P2);\n    var minx=Infinity, maxx=-Infinity, miny=Infinity, maxy=-Infinity;\n    for(var i=0;i<all.length;i++){\n      var x=all[i][0], y=all[i][1];\n      if(x<minx) minx=x; if(x>maxx) maxx=x;\n      if(y<miny) miny=y; if(y>maxy) maxy=y;\n    }\n    var cx=(minx+maxx)/2, cy=(miny+maxy)/2;\n    var half = Math.max((maxx-minx)/2, (maxy-miny)/2, 1.0)*1.35 + 0.15;\n    return { cx:cx, cy:cy, half:half };\n  }\n\n  function drawPanel(cv, pts, color, labelColor){\n    var rect = cv.getBoundingClientRect();\n    var dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n    var W = Math.max(1, rect.width), H = Math.max(1, rect.height);\n    var pw = Math.round(W*dpr), ph = Math.round(H*dpr);\n    if(cv.width !== pw || cv.height !== ph){ cv.width = pw; cv.height = ph; }\n    var ctx = cv.getContext('2d');\n    ctx.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0);\n    ctx.clearRect(0,0,W,H);\n\n    var sc = Math.min(W,H)/(2*view.half);\n    var px = function(x){ return W/2 + (x - view.cx)*sc; };\n    var py = function(y){ return H/2 - (y - view.cy)*sc; };\n\n    /* faint grid */\n    var halfX = (W/2)/sc, halfY = (H/2)/sc;\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#eef1f5';\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    var gx0 = Math.ceil(view.cx - halfX), gx1 = Math.floor(view.cx + halfX);\n    for(var gx=gx0; gx<=gx1; gx++){\n      var X = Math.round(px(gx)) + 0.5;\n      ctx.moveTo(X, 0); ctx.lineTo(X, H);\n    }\n    var gy0 = Math.ceil(view.cy - halfY), gy1 = Math.floor(view.cy + halfY);\n    for(var gy=gy0; gy<=gy1; gy++){\n      var Y = Math.round(py(gy)) + 0.5;\n      ctx.moveTo(0, Y); ctx.lineTo(W, Y);\n    }\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    /* axes */\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#d3d9e1';\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    if(view.cx - halfX < 0 && view.cx + halfX > 0){\n      var ax = Math.round(px(0)) + 0.5;\n      ctx.moveTo(ax, 0); ctx.lineTo(ax, H);\n    }\n    if(view.cy - halfY < 0 && view.cy + halfY > 0){\n      var ay = Math.round(py(0)) + 0.5;\n      ctx.moveTo(0, ay); ctx.lineTo(W, ay);\n    }\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    /* pairwise lines */\n    ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(17,24,39,0.14)';\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    for(var i=0;i<pts.length;i++) for(var j=i+1;j<pts.length;j++){\n      ctx.moveTo(px(pts[i][0]), py(pts[i][1]));\n      ctx.lineTo(px(pts[j][0]), py(pts[j][1]));\n    }\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    /* points + labels */\n    ctx.font = '700 12px -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif';\n    ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';\n    for(var m=0;m<pts.length;m++){\n      var sx = px(pts[m][0]), sy = py(pts[m][1]);\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.arc(sx, sy, 6, 0, Math.PI*2);\n      ctx.fillStyle = color;\n      ctx.fill();\n      ctx.lineWidth = 2;\n      ctx.strokeStyle = '#ffffff';\n      ctx.stroke();\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = labelColor;\n      var lx = sx + 10, ly = sy - 10;\n      if(lx > W - 14) lx = sx - 20;\n      if(ly < 10) ly = sy + 14;\n      ctx.fillText(LABELS[m], lx, ly);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function loop(){\n    var t = computeTargetView();\n    if(!view.init){\n      view.cx = t.cx; view.cy = t.cy; view.half = t.half; view.init = true;\n    } else {\n      var a = 0.2;\n      view.cx   += (t.cx   - view.cx)*a;\n      view.cy   += (t.cy   - view.cy)*a;\n      view.half += (t.half - view.half)*a;\n    }\n    drawPanel(cvA, points,     '#2563eb', '#1d4ed8');\n    drawPanel(cvB, current.P2, '#ea7317', '#c2410c');\n    requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- events ---------------- */\n  thetaEl.addEventListener('input', function(){ state.theta = parseFloat(thetaEl.value); syncUI(); update(); });\n  shearEl.addEventListener('input', function(){ state.shear = parseFloat(shearEl.value); syncUI(); update(); });\n  scaleEl.addEventListener('input', function(){ state.scale = parseFloat(scaleEl.value); syncUI(); update(); });\n\n  modeBtns.forEach(function(b){\n    b.addEventListener('click', function(){ state.mode = b.dataset.mode; syncUI(); update(); });\n  });\n\n  presetBtns.forEach(function(b){\n    b.addEventListener('click', function(){\n      var p = b.dataset.preset;\n      if(p === 'rot37'){ state.mode='rotation'; state.theta=37; }\n      else if(p === 'shear08'){ state.mode='shear'; state.shear=0.8; }\n      else if(p === 'rotshear'){ state.mode='rotshear'; state.theta=40; state.shear=0.7; }\n      syncUI(); update();\n    });\n  });\n\n  function randomizePoints(){\n    var pts = [], guard = 0;\n    while(pts.length < N && guard < 40000){\n      guard++;\n      var x = 0.25 + Math.random()*3;\n      var y = 0.25 + Math.random()*3;\n      var ok = true;\n      for(var i=0;i<pts.length;i++){\n        if(Math.hypot(pts[i][0]-x, pts[i][1]-y) < 0.55){ ok = false; break; }\n      }\n      if(ok) pts.push([x,y]);\n    }\n    points = (pts.length === N) ? pts : DEFAULT_POINTS.map(function(p){ return p.slice(); });\n    update();\n  }\n  $('randomBtn').addEventListener('click', randomizePoints);\n\n  /* ---------------- boot ---------------- */\n  syncUI();\n  update();\n  requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n\n  /* expose a tiny hook for automated checks */\n  window.__demo = {\n    getQ:getQ,\n    readouts:function(){\n      return {\n        gram: $('gramChange').textContent,\n        dist: $('distChange').textContent,\n        verdict: $('verdict').textContent,\n        mode: state.mode\n      };\n    },\n    setState:function(s){\n      for(var k in s){ if(k in state) state[k] = s[k]; }\n      syncUI(); update();\n    }\n  };\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
		"tested": true,
		"notes": "All tests pass (no console errors; rotation reads 0.00%/0.00% orthogonal, shear 0.8 reads ~118% Gram change and ~43% distance change with det = 1.0000, scale k=1 correctly reads orthogonal, rotation×shear at det = 1 reads non-orthogonal).\n\n**Notes for the teacher:** Two same-scale panels show the fixed 6-point cloud (A–F, faint grey pairwise lines) and the same cloud after Q, with a \"randomize points\" button for fresh configurations. Controls: mode selector (rotation / shear / scaling / rotation × shear, with the inactive sliders visibly greyed out), θ 0–360°, shear s ∈ [−1.5, 1.5] with a prominent live \"det S = 1.00\", scale k ∈ [0.5, 2], the live 2×2 Q, and three presets. Readouts: the big max-relative-change percentages for the Gram matrix and for pairwise distances, K and K′ as side-by-side 6×6 heatmaps (hover any cell to compare K_ij, K′_ij, Δ in both), and a verdict line plus ‖QᵀQ − I‖_F and det(Q) in the non-orthogonal case. Try: rotation preset → 0.00%/0.00% and the \"orthogonal\" verdict; then the \"shear 0.8 (det = 1)\" preset → det stays 1.000 but both readouts jump, which is the caption's counterexample; also note scaling with k = 1 counts as orthogonal."
